 *  - The Files tab already browses the customer's WHOLE guest as root (their own VM), so there is
 *    no "allowed root" narrower than "/" to enforce: what a user may download is exactly what they
 *    may already list. What we DO enforce: absolute, normalised paths with no ".." (normalizePath),
 *    single-segment names for archive members, a deny-list of virtual filesystems for archives
 *    (/proc, /sys, /dev: infinite or meaningless "files"), regular files only for single downloads
 *    (never a device node / fifo), and hard byte / file-count caps.
